course: dictionary
lesson: 15688
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. «The ting of the bell told us that lunch was ready.» Here ting is a noun: a short, high, clear ringing sound.
explain: Ting can also be a verb, which means to make that sound. «When Sam tapped the glass, it tinged once.» Tinged is the past tense of ting, so the glass made a small, bright sound. Ask yourself: is the word a thing, or is it an action?
explain: In London speech, ting can mean «thing». «What's that ting on your desk?» means «What's that thing on your desk?» This is slang, so use it when talking with friends, not in your school writing.
explain: Ting is a sound word. It sounds like the noise it describes, like the ting of a bicycle bell or a microwave. Writers use sound words to help the reader hear the story.
fact: Ting is a noun for a short, high, clear ringing sound, like a small bell.
fact: Ting is also a verb: to ting means to make that ringing sound.
fact: Sound words like ting are called onomatopoeia, because they sound like what they mean.
fact: In UK youth slang from London and Jamaican speech, «ting» means «thing».
fact: Slang is informal, so it is best kept for chatting with friends, not for school writing.
exercise: «I heard a clear ting from the bicycle bell.» What is ting in this sentence? | A friend's name | A slow, deep drum beat | A type of bicycle | *A short, high ringing sound
exercise: «What's that ting on your desk?» In this slang, what does ting mean? | A song | *A thing | A bird | A bell
exercise: «The glass tinged when the spoon touched it.» What did the glass do? | *Made a short, clear ringing sound | Broke into pieces | Filled with water | Turned cold
test: «The ting of the doorbell made the dog bark.» What is the ting? | A type of door | A soft blanket | *A short, high ringing sound | A loud shout
test: «Can you pass me that ting?» In this slang, what does ting mean? | A song | *A thing | A bell | A cold drink
exam: «Nina heard a ting and stopped to listen.» What kind of word is ting here? | A place | A verb meaning to run | *A noun for a short, high ringing sound | A colour
